  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Breezy conditions this afternoon, with \ngusts to 25-35 mph (strongest winds in Eastern Nevada). Elevated \nfire weather conditions during the day as dry conditions will leave \nhumidity below 15%, however remain borderline as when the winds \nincrease, humidity also rises above 20% due to the much cooler \ntemperatures moving in. Highs will be several degrees below normal \nfor Northern Nevada in the 70s with Central Nevada staying in the \n80s. Overnight lows will be coldest in Northern Nevada in the 30s \nwith some areas dropping to freezing level, while Central Nevada \ncools into the 40s. \n\nMonday, winds are expected to be light and fair as the main\nfrontal passage moves northeast along with the jet streak. A\nweak shortwave trough pattern will remain over the northwestern \nCONUS behind the low pressure system which will keep a near zonal \nto almost northwesterly flow over Nevada. This will keep \ntemperatures cooler across central and northern Nevada with highs \nin the 60s to 70s. Overnight lows will also remain cool with \nnorthern Nevada again in the 30s (some areas reaching to freezing \ntemperatures) and central Nevada in the 40s. \n\nTuesday and through the week, there is some inconsistencies \nwithin the forecast as to what transpires with the upper level \ntrough, with some models showing the trough strengthening to a low\npressure system and moving over Nevada, while others show the \ntrough remaining unchanged. The main consistency is that \ntemperatures will gradually warm back to near normal throughout \nthe week with highs staying in the upper 70s to 80s until reaching\nabove normal by next weekend. Winds will also be consistent \nstaying light to some mild afternoon breezes. No weather is \nforecasted throughout the week.",
